    <div class="pm-r4-wrap"><div class="pm-r4">
      <article class="pm-r4-card" data-p="s">
        <div class="pm-r4-head"><span class="pm-r4-n">1</span><h2>Seven Behaviors</h2></div>
        <div class="pm-r4-who"><img src="/img/nielson-traitors/pundit-s.png" alt=""><span class="pm-r4-name">Dr. Solveig "The Lie Detector" Bergqvist</span>
          <p class="pm-r4-says">The shield and every secret condition now use the same seven behaviors. One short list makes patterns much easier to track.</p></div>
        <table class="pm-r4-table"><tbody>
          <tr><td>Chatty</td><td>8+ messages</td></tr><tr><td>Quiet</td><td>Only 1 or 2 messages</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Early</td><td>A post in the first 10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Late</td><td>A post in the final 2 hours</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Reactor</td><td>10+ reactions to others</td></tr><tr><td>Tagger</td><td>Tag another player</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Long</td><td>One message of 250+ characters</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="pm-r4-ex"><b>Example</b><p>You send 9 messages in today's mission. That's Chatty. If today's shield is for the most messages and nobody sends more, the shield is yours.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pm-r4-card" data-p="d">
        <div class="pm-r4-head"><span class="pm-r4-n">2</span><h2>Intel With History</h2></div>
        <div class="pm-r4-who"><img src="/img/nielson-traitors/pundit-d.png" alt=""><span class="pm-r4-name">Desmond "The Archive" Oyelaran</span>
          <p class="pm-r4-says">Every morning you'll learn a behavior another player demonstrated in the previous round and how often they've done it before. Someone is learning yours too. It's my binder in a DM.</p></div>
        <ol class="pm-r4-list">
          <li>Every active player gets one fact written about them</li><li>Who gets the fact about you is random</li>
          <li>Hitting none of the behaviors in box 1 is a fact too</li><li>Each game starts with a DM of your own history</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="pm-r4-ex"><b>Example</b><p>&ldquo;Tariq was Early with a post 3 minutes in. Tariq has been Early in 2 of 14 past missions.&rdquo; Tariq is rarely Early, so that's worth noticing.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pm-r4-card" data-p="t">
        <div class="pm-r4-head"><span class="pm-r4-n">3</span><h2>The Seer Rotates</h2></div>
        <div class="pm-r4-who"><img src="/img/nielson-traitors/pundit-t.png" alt=""><span class="pm-r4-name">Tariq "Wake Up" Haddad</span>
          <p class="pm-r4-says">Nobody is the Seer full-time, and the Bodyguard is folded in. Each round the bot secretly picks a new Seer. Why you? I have theories.</p></div>
        <ol class="pm-r4-list">
          <li>Meet your secret condition from box 1 that day</li><li>That night: check a player OR protect one</li>
          <li>Multiple Seers have different information</li><li>Protect when one murder could end the game</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="pm-r4-ex"><b>Example</b><p>Your DM says you're the Seer and your condition is Early. You post 5 minutes in. Tonight you can check Solveig or protect Solveig.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pm-r4-card" data-p="p">
        <div class="pm-r4-head"><span class="pm-r4-n">4</span><h2>Traitor Conditions</h2></div>
        <div class="pm-r4-who"><img src="/img/nielson-traitors/pundit-p.png" alt=""><span class="pm-r4-name">Lady Parveen "The Velvet Dagger" Chaudhry-Montague</span>
          <p class="pm-r4-says">Each Traitor gets one condition from box 1 for the whole game, darlings. There's a murder each night as long as one of us met ours that day.</p></div>
        <ol class="pm-r4-list">
          <li>Same condition in every mission</li><li>Partners draw different types and know both</li>
          <li>If neither Traitor meets theirs, nobody dies</li><li>A recruit who says yes draws their own condition</li>
        </ol>
